.TH SPECTRO 1 "October 2026" "Spectro" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
spectro \- spectral-state guided audio synthesis workbench
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spectro
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B spectro-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
Spectro learns spectral structure from audio with linear prediction and a
hidden Markov model, then synthesizes new audio from the learned states.
The desktop workbench provides training, model loading, generation, and visual
audio inspection. All processing runs locally.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B train
Train a model from audio files or directories and save an NPZ or safetensors model.
.TP
.B generate
Load a model and render a WAV file with a chosen duration, sample rate, and seed.
.TP
.B adapt
Update an existing model from additional recordings with bounded training memory,
then export a new model.
.TP
.B inspect
Display model information. Use \fB\-\-json\fR for machine-readable output.
.TP
.B demo
Train on a synthetic example and render audio without supplying recordings.
.TP
.B doctor
Report dependency versions and native backend availability.
.TP
.B gui
Open the desktop workbench.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBspectro \-\-help\fR or \fBspectro command \-\-help\fR for the complete
options accepted by the installed version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
spectro train ./recordings --output voice.npz
spectro generate voice.npz --output result.wav --duration 5 --seed 42
spectro adapt voice.npz ./new-recordings --output updated.npz
spectro inspect voice.npz --json
spectro demo --output-dir ./spectro-demo
spectro-gui
.fi
.SH FILES
.I /usr/lib/spectro
contains the application and compiled native kernels.
.br
.I /usr/share/doc/spectro
contains the license and installation documentation.
